  <metadata>
    <name>Lakeland Way — Clockwise day 7 (2026-09-06)</name>
    <desc>Base 17.6km, +811m; with 6 detour(s): +12.3km, +803m ascent. Total 29.9km.</desc>
  </metadata>
  <wpt lat="54.515412" lon="-2.877346">
    <ele>696.0</ele>
    <name>Rest Dodd 696m</name>
    <desc>A 696m fell on the Martindale side of the High Street ridge. Detour: +1.6km, +159m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.513781" lon="-2.854141">
    <ele>802.0</ele>
    <name>High Raise (High Street) 802m</name>
    <desc>An 802m broad top, the highest of the far eastern fells after High Street. Detour: +3.0km, +144m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.507436" lon="-2.861731">
    <ele>792.0</ele>
    <name>Rampsgill Head 792m</name>
    <desc>A 792m top with crags falling into Rampsgill, beside Kidsty Pike. Detour: +1.2km, +73m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.505683" lon="-2.855517">
    <ele>780.0</ele>
    <name>Kidsty Pike 780m</name>
    <desc>A 780m top with a neat peaked profile above Riggindale, overlooking Haweswater. Detour: +2.2km, +86m ascent.</desc>
    <type>peaks</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.502068" lon="-2.879572">
    <ele>428.0</ele>
    <name>Hayeswater</name>
    <desc>A former reservoir at 428m under Gray Crag, now returned to a natural tarn. Detour: +0.3km, +0m ascent.</desc>
    <type>wild-swim-spots</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.488920" lon="-2.852351">
    <ele>486.0</ele>
    <name>Blea Water</name>
    <desc>The deepest tarn in England at around 63m, held in a textbook glacial corrie under High Street at 486m. Very cold, very clear, with a boulder shore and no easy shallows. Detour: +3.9km, +341m ascent.</desc>
    <type>wild-swim-spots</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="54.481241" lon="-2.873929">
    <name>Night 7 — camp</name>
    <type>camp</type>
  </wpt>
